# A project agent container image: the workspace toolchain image with this daemon as its entrypoint.
#
# This is the shape an agent container actually runs — the toolchain the project's checkout needs,
# with the daemon as PID 1 — assembled from the two halves that own themselves. The toolchain is not
# built here and could not be: reproducing it would put node, maven and a native toolchain in a repo
# whose rule is that a clone alone builds green with no monorepo and no docker.
#
# THE BASE IS `qits/workspace-base`, WHICH IS NOW A RELEASED IMAGE. It used to default to
# `qits/workspace:latest`, the name a hand-built toolchain carried on one machine before the layered
# workspace image took that name. The toolchain lives in `images/qits-oci-workspace` now and CI
# publishes it, so the base is a name with a history behind it rather than whatever was last built
# locally. `qits/workspace` is the wrong base either way: it is the same toolchain with the
# *workspace* daemon layered on, so taking it would carry a second binary this image never runs.
#
# BOTH ARGS ARE UNQUALIFIED AND BOTH ARE OVERRIDDEN BY CI. No registry-qualified reference is
# portable here — the registry is `qits-platform-artifacts:8080` inside a step container and
# `localhost:8081` outside — so the defaults name what a developer's machine can resolve and
# anything building for real passes a qualified, version-pinned value, which is what
# `.config/qits/ci-event-release.yml` does:
#
#     docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.projects \
#       --build-arg BASE=localhost:8081/qits/workspace-base:<version> \
#       --build-arg DAEMON_IMAGE=localhost:8081/qits/projects-daemon:<version> \
#       -t localhost:8081/qits/project-agent:<version> .
#
# Build the daemon image first when working from local tags:
#
#     docker build -t qits/projects-daemon:latest -f docker/Dockerfile .
#     docker build -t qits/project-agent:native -f docker/Dockerfile.projects .
#
# --- BASE CARRIES A LITERAL VERSION, AND THAT IS THE TOOLCHAIN PIN ---------------------------------
# The version in `ARG BASE` is not decoration on a convenience default: it IS the committed pin, and
# it lives here rather than in a file beside the pipeline because qits-maintenance reads literal
# `ARG <NAME>=<image>:<tag>` Dockerfile defaults as docker pins — this one at `arg:BASE`, matched on
# the bare `qits/workspace-base` — and its bump pipeline rewrites this line's tag when the toolchain
# releases. It used to be `.config/qits/workspace-base.version`, one line moved by a hop pipeline in
# this repository; the hop is gone and the pin moved into the line the build already reads.
#
# WHICH IS WHY `.config/qits/ci-event-release.yml` NOW DERIVES ITS `--build-arg BASE=` FROM THIS
# LINE. The property the file gave up must not be lost with it: the release pipeline reads the pin
# out of the RELEASED tree, so rebuilding a tag rebuilds on exactly the toolchain that tag shipped
# with, rather than on whatever is newest. A floating tag would break that — and there is none to
# follow anyway, since qits-workspace-oci publishes only `:<version>`.
#
# KEEP THE VALUE LITERAL. A `$`, a `@`, a `://`, or a tag with no `/` before it each make maintenance
# stop seeing a pin here. Nothing would fail; the base would just quietly stop following the
# toolchain forever.
#
# --- DAEMON_IMAGE IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* A PIN -----------------------------------------------------
# The `${DAEMON_VERSION}` indirection is load-bearing and the whole reason DAEMON_VERSION exists.
# This ARG names THIS repository's own artifact, and a literal `qits/projects-daemon:<version>` here
# would be read as a docker pin like any other — so every release of this repository would make its
# own Dockerfile outdated and maintenance would open a bump proposing this repository follow itself,
# forever. Docker pins have no reactor-own exclusion the way maven coordinates do, so the exclusion
# has to be written in the value: a `$` is never a pin.
#
# The default still resolves to `qits/projects-daemon:latest` for a developer, and CI overrides
# DAEMON_IMAGE wholesale with the reference it just pushed, so nothing about the build changes.
# DAEMON_VERSION is not meant to be passed by hand; override DAEMON_IMAGE, as the release does.
# --- why BASE is the FULL workspace toolchain -----------------------------------------------------
# A leaner base was on the table: a project agent's own job is git plus a coding-agent CLI, and it
# runs no dev server of its own. It takes the whole toolchain anyway, because the agent's job is to
# work on the project's code — build it, test it, run its tooling — and a base that cannot compile
# the project makes the agent useless at the thing it exists for. Trimming it would also fork the
# toolchain: two images to keep in step, and a build failure that only reproduces in one of them.
ARG BASE=qits/workspace-base:2026.902.143920
ARG DAEMON_VERSION=latest
ARG DAEMON_IMAGE=qits/projects-daemon:${DAEMON_VERSION}

FROM ${DAEMON_IMAGE} AS daemon

FROM ${BASE}
COPY --from=daemon /work/qits-projects-daemon /usr/local/bin/qits-projects-daemon

# Replaces whatever the base entrypoints to. No CMD and no `sleep infinity` fallback: a container
# whose daemon cannot start is not a usable agent, and should fail visibly rather than idle looking
# healthy.
ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/qits-projects-daemon"]
